      "side": 1,
      "message": "gpio_list[] is extracted from gpio.inc(through gpio.wrap) by expanding macro GPIO(). It\u0027s of struct type as below. As a result, GPIO_PIN has to provide port and mask, here GPIO_0 is used as port. GPIO_0 is essentially 0 since we only have port 0 for ISH GPIO port.\n\n\nstruct gpio_info {\n\t/* Signal name */\n\tconst char *name;\n\n\t/* Port base address */\n\tuint32_t port;\n\n\t/* Bitmask on that port (1 \u003c\u003c N; 0 \u003d signal not implemented) */\n\tuint32_t mask;\n\n\t/* Flags (GPIO_*; see above) */\n\tuint32_t flags;\n};\n\n\n#define GPIO(name, pin, flags) {#name, GPIO_##pin, flags},\n#define GPIO_INT(name, pin, flags, signal) GPIO(name, pin, flags)\n\n/* GPIO signal list. */\nconst struct gpio_info gpio_list[] \u003d {\n\t#include \"gpio.wrap\"            \n};",
